ation": "The pool gate log (.prawduct/pool-kairo-b20657ffa.txt) records 1 failure: tests/enforcement/test_api_growth_requires_a_minor_bump.py::test_the_workspace_declares_an_honest_version ('the version 0.85.0 is BELOW the latest release v0.86.0'). It fails because develop was tagged v0.86.0 after this branch last merged develop, not because of code in the interval. The protocol rates a test failure in the evidence BLOCKING, so it is rated here. The builder's brief records a user ruling that the version and the develop merge are left to the maintainer. Either record that ruling as this finding's disposition, or merge develop so the workspace version is no longer behind the latest tag. Do not weaken the test. Scope: instance.", "files": ["tests/enforcement/test_api_growth_requires_a_minor_bump.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "test-status is stale: no .test-evidence.json on disk", "recommendation": "`prawduct-hook test-status` exits 1 with 'stale: no .test-evidence.json on disk'. That exit code is the only freshness signal, so the pool log and the integration figures in the brief do not count as recorded evidence. Record test evidence for b20657ffa through the project's evidence path before the PR lands. Scope: instance.", "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "measure_value_misfit lets any value through for an untyped measure, but the bundle summarises an untyped measure as numeric, so text under one now crashes the analysis", "recommendation": "The removed bundle/measures.py `_value_fits` treated `data_type=None` as numeric: it accepted only a non-bool number. The new `kernel/metrics.measure_value_misfit` returns None (fits) for any value when `descriptor.data_type is None`. `_verdict` now pools any such value once `_is_reportable` holds (`higher_is_better` set or `diagnostic=True`). The summariser in bundle/measures.py (the `else:` branch, `observed = [float(value) for value i