d findings and `not draft`. Also, the test module's docstring 'refused, review_failed and failed store nothing' is no longer true after a cleared review. Make that line relational (unless a cleared review sent the revision) or delete it. Scope: instance.", "files": ["packages/evals/tests/test_report_writer_loop.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/loop.py"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "record_lint suite-total-claim on r2-config-sweep.md is a false positive", "recommendation": "record_lint flags '200 test' at packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/analyst/skill/exemplars/r2-config-sweep.md:3. The line says '1,200 test cases graded by exact match', which is the synthetic reference eval's dataset size, not a test-suite total. Nothing reads it as a suite count, and no edit is wanted. Also unchecked: chunk-ref-missing graded chunk A by inference, because the dispatch carried no chunk. That is cumulative-mode bookkeeping, not a defect. Scope: none.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/analyst/skill/exemplars/r2-config-sweep.md"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "Multi-aspect tables re-implement the lead aspect's cell readers in a second path, and the per-aspect helpers are themselves copied across modules", "recommendation": "Class, bounded to the multi-aspect reading in analysis/report. Gap A put a second implementation next to the one-aspect path instead of making the lead aspect one case of a per-aspect reader. (1) tables._board is a verbatim copy of figure_keys._aspect_board, docstring included. (2) tables._aspect_pass_rate and full_results._aspect_pass_rate are the same function: one reads through tables._count/_figure, the other through a new full_results._figure_value that repeats tables._figure's try/except UnresolvableReference with its own NOSILENT comment. (3) tables._aspect_cost/_aspect_costs repeat the branches of _a